  "note": "Dedicated standalone cold/warm, perceived-input/EventTiming calibration, heap/GC characterization and adverse-visualization measurement smoke entries are explicitly deferred; they are not passes. Ordinary component, input, visual, runtime lifecycle, privacy and security suites remain required. Owner override 2026-09-13: performance qualification is DEFERRED, not passed, and nonblocking for launch. Original numeric budgets and manual benchmark commands remain unchanged. The command ledger retains non-timed planner/reducer/browser correctness, installed package graph security, and cleanup/adverse/DOM functional checks. Observational values in functional smoke reports are not performance qualification. Correctness, security, source integrity, package and other release checks remain required. Every implemented package test script is indexed except test:data-stream (alias of test:data) and test:visualization:temporal:browser (already included by test:visualization:browser). The deterministic public-API scenario suite is an explicit unit gate; it proves only the scenario IDs named by its assertions. Source lint first proves its active configuration rejects a known correctness violation, then runs Oxlint correctness rules across packages, apps, examples and scripts, followed by TypeScript unused-local/parameter checks across packages, examples and the local Studio. Deliberate control-character validation regexes and three reviewed Unicorn rewrite rules are disabled explicitly. The separate Prettier gate covers workspace/package/workflow configuration plus the public-docs, release, platform-fixture, and associated test surfaces; it does not claim whole-repository formatting. Release, publication, bootstrap-preflight, and docs producers share a tested source-state contract that rejects non-ignored untracked inputs before assigning a clean source identity. Security and static module boundaries remain required; installed byte and Node/browser timing qualification are deferred by owner. Historical timing failures are retained; current qualification is deferred by owner. The non-timed Node and browser functional commands run together before the visual corpus, and the CI runner stops at the first failed command after persisting its partial failed ledger. Standalone, perceived-input and heap-lifecycle smoke collect cache/DOM/heap observations without a timing-budget or leak qualification claim. Website page, navigation, layout and deployment checks are owned by the private Arconath/aeliqo-site repository after the split. Historical T27/S63 evidence remains explicitly pre-split and is not rebound to current public source. Human/live integrated evidence remains required; performance qualification is deferred. The visual corpus is executed as three sequential browser-project commands with isolated output directories; each retains the existing 3600-second timeout. This changes the visual worst-case allowance from 3600 to 10800 seconds, while the workflow-level 180-minute cap remains unchanged. No case, browser, assertion, or performance budget is removed.",
